# The probe files this course's artifact writes while it works.
#
# The `_NNN` files are the one-instruction-per-file probes: a batch of fifty
# probes in one .s means the single probe the assembler rejects takes the other
# forty-nine with it, and a run that prints blanks looks exactly like a run that
# measured nothing.  They are the residue of that discipline and they are not
# part of the course.
_*.s
_*.o
__pycache__/

# The generated .s and .o are here rather than ignored because they ARE the
# course: every instruction count in section 5 is a claim about a line of
# these files, and every two-reader agreement in section 11 is a claim about a
# word in the .o.  `build_samples.sh` rebuilds all thirteen of them from two C
# files in about a second, and `crosscheck.py` reads the SHIPPED ones, so a
# reader can check the claims without a compiler at all.
